{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794374077000-engineer-cc3-fix-r2.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-11 08:47:57 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 15:47:57 +0700\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: d6c85345-2ddd-42b1-8272-04edf1de6cc9\nModel: muse-wonder-1.0\n\n# cc3 fix round r2 — reconcile the astra review (4×P1, 2×P2): findings\n\nStatus: COMPLETE — all six accepted items fixed and verified in the\nuncommitted eight-file diff on `cc3-lowering-provenance` (base `ced9f2c2`).\nNothing committed. The r2 changes touch only three of the eight files:\n`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`, `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`,\n`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`. No forbidden file was edited\n(`macro.cljc`, `ast_walker.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`, `yang/clojure.cljc`,\n`core/prelude.cljc`, `dht.cljc`, `index.cljc` untouched); canonical bytes,\nhashes, and guest-instruction counts are unchanged (provenance remains\nhost-side side artifacts only).\n\n## Per-finding disposition\n\n### 1. P1 — stamped paths ≠ pre-stamp paths (latte_oracle_test.clj) — FIXED\n\n- `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3479` `cc3-correspond`: the explicit\n  stamped→pre-stamp transformation mapping. Both trees are traversed\n  together in grammar positions; recognized stamping wrappers\n  (`kernel-stamped-args?` — the three applications a stamp inserts around\n  an argument node) are removed by descending to the wrapped argument at\n  `operands[0]/operands[1]/operands[2]`. A type mismatch, a child-count\n  mismatch, a wrapper over a pre-stamp wrapper, or a site with no\n  correspondence refuses with `:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence`; two\n  sites mapping to one occurrence refuse with\n  `:rule :cc3-ambiguous-stamp-correspondence`. A mapped key that is no\n  validated C1 occurrence also refuses at binding time.\n- `cc3-oracle-binding` (`:3555`) now combines the PRE-STAMP root only\n  with correspondence-translated paths, and returns `:correspondence`\n  and `:stamped-paths` as evidence.\n- Tests: `test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested` (`:3799`, synthetic: a\n  guest call nested inside another stamped call's argument vector really\n  moves — pre-stamp `[[3 1] [3 1]]` vs a longer stamped path — and maps\n  back to its own application; divergent trees refuse), plus the\n  binding deftest's correspondence assertion for every bound site.\n\n### 2. P1 — synthesized origin from content (latte_oracle_test.clj) — FIXED\n\n- `kernel-compile` records the admission coordinate WHEN ADMITTING the\n  fixture (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2451` counter, `:2472`\n  record): the batch token is `<canonical-source-hash>#admission-<n>`\n  with `n` the harness's sequential admission ordinal, retained with the\n  compilation as `:admission-origin`. Identical content admitted twice\n  is two histories with two origins; the content hash alone is never the\n  origin.\n- `cc3-oracle-binding` consumes ONLY that retained record: a compilation\n  without one refuses with `:rule :cc3-admission-record`; no new envelope\n  is synthesized post-compilation, and `[:oracle/fixture <id>]` is still\n  never minted.\n- Tests: the binding deftest pins origin = retained record, origin ≠\n  content-only coordinate, missing-record refusal, and replay (rebinding\n  one retained compilation answers the identical binding).\n  `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` (`:3837`) pins two\n  admissions of identical content (same canonical hash) carrying\n  distinct origins, with the same sites bound under each admission's own\n  origin.\n\n### 3. P1 — root-only lookup borrows across admissions (repl.cljc) — FIXED\n\n- `packet-call-provenance` (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:172`) is now\n  `[state packet admission]`: it requires the packet's retained\n  admission identity, validates it (`:rule :call-site-admission` for a\n  malformed identity), and selects the retained table by\n  `[admission root]` exactly. An admission with no claim for the root\n  answers nil — aligning with `record-call-site-admissions`' refusal to\n  assign old evidence to new programs (repl.cljc:~1425 in the new\n  numbering). The old root-only scan and its ambiguous-across-admissions\n  branch are gone (a map keyed `[admission root]` cannot be ambiguous\n  under one admission).\n- Regression in `repl-packet-call-provenance-test`\n  (`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2013`): claimed-A/unclaimed-B\n  with an identical root — B answers nil; two retained admissions for\n  one root each resolve their own rows; malformed admission refuses.\n\n### 4. P1 — REPL provenance still not persisted (repl.cljc) — FIXED\n\n- Production connection: `eval-program` records this round's claims —\n  roots the expander newly retained under exactly one admission — as\n  `:call-site-round-claims` (`repl.cljc:1964`); `run-evaluator-stage`\n  wraps EVERY production loader (`:1484 retaining-load`) so a claimed\n  packet's provenance is durably retained at load time, on the ordinary\n  REPL path (all four evaluators, since all go through this stage). The\n  transient round-claims key is dissociated from the resulting state.\n- Retention: `retain-packet-call-provenance!` (`repl.cljc:218`)\n  materializes the relation\n  `{:yin.vm.provenance/schema 1 :admission … :root … :semantic/:stack/\n  :register …}` and a `{:yin.repl.call-provenance/schema 1 …}` record\n  naming it into the session's `:index-store` (the durable `dao.jing`\n  handle), both content-addressed side artifacts outside any manifest\n  hash — extending the module-publication pattern, not duplicating it.\n  `call-provenance-handles` (`:282`) exposes the session's\n  `{[admission root] record-address}` lookup handles;\n  `retained-packet-call-provenance` (`:251`) retrieves and verifies a\n  relation by handle alone.\n- Test: `repl-packet-provenance-durable-test`\n  (`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2055`, JVM lane): a real\n  session over `{:type :file :dir …}` evaluates three inputs through\n  `repl/eval-input`, retains handles, closes the store, reopens it with\n  `yin.repl.store/open`, and retrieves the identical relation by handle.\n\n### 5. P2 — complete transformed coverage + multiplicities — FIXED\n\n- The binding now also projects the STAMPED tree (`cc3-oracle-binding`\n  returns `:stamped-tree/:stamped-rows/:stamped-marked/\n  :stamped-eligible`). The binding deftest verifies the\n  POST-transformation application set separately from oracle sites: the\n  stamped set (987) is exactly the marked occurrences (981) plus the\n  independently derived inserted helpers (one wrapper per site × three\n  applications: `data/nth`, `dsg__intra_call`, `conj`), disjoint from the\n  marked set — inserted helpers are accounted for as their own set, not\n  silently marked or silently dropped.\n- Multiplicities: the lowering block now compares FREQUENCIES, not key\n  sets — semantic/stack/register call-provenance multisets each equal\n  the independently derived expected multiset (every marked application\n  of the compiled tree except Rule-R `yin/def` applications, derived by\n  walking the compiled map AST), and the provenance PCs equal exactly\n  the `:call` PCs of each image in pc order (semantic vector, stack\n  image, register instructions). Rule-R (`:define`) occurrences remain\n  excluded from call events. Measured on the pinned fixture: 948 call\n  rows = 981 marked − 33 Rule-R definitions.\n\n### 6. P2 — preflight record incomplete under design §6.3 — FIXED (record below)\n\nSee PREFLIGHT BOUNDS (r2). The earlier run's status is preserved\nverbatim there: the r1 preflight (compile-only counts, restated\n4,000,000/1,000,000 ceilings) was and remains INCOMPLETE under §6.3; it\nis not re-stamped as preflight-complete. The r2 record adds the missing\nmeasured quantities and finite ceilings BEFORE any fresh tagged\nevidence in this round was taken (the measurements are compile/binding/\nlowering only; the tagged deftest runs below cite this record).\n\n## PREFLIGHT BOUNDS (r2; design §6.3)\n\nPreserved status of the earlier run: the cc3 r1 preflight record\n(1,316 stamped rows / 3,669 occurrences / 987 stamped applications /\nmax path depth 90 / 103,650 path bytes / restated 4,000,000 guest\ninstructions and 1,000,000 trace records per C lane) supplied NO\nstatic-side storage or retained-memory bound, NO compilation/\npublication/verification time ceilings, and NO process/heap ceiling or\nmeasurement method. It stands in the r1 findings as an\nincomplete-preflight run; nothing here re-stamps it.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-11 in-session (JVM, warm; fixture\n`{:call (latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` through\n`kernel-compile`, `cc3-oracle-binding`, `linearize/project-rows`,\n`derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image`; bytes are\n`dao.jing/canonical-bytes` lengths; heap by\n`java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime` `totalMemory − freeMemory`, sampled in\nthe measuring JVM after binding — a process-wide figure including the\ntest harness, comparable only on this host/JVM):\n\n| Bound | Measured | Declared finite ceiling |\n|---|---|---|\n| Canonical rows (pre-stamp tree) | 1,309 | — (r1 record) |\n| Application occurrences A (pre-stamp / stamped) | 981 / 987 | — (r1 record) |\n| Oracle sites | 2 | — |\n| Call-provenance rows (semantic) | 948 | — |\n| Static side bytes: C1 rows (canonical) | 332,846 B | — |\n| Static side bytes: provenance relation, all 3 lanes (canonical) | 927,196 B | 2,000,000 B per artifact (rows + relation) |\n| Retained memory (relation retained per artifact) | 927,196 B canonical | 1,000,000 B per artifact; 8,000,000 B aggregate session closure |\n| Compilation time (`kernel-compile`, warm JVM) | 79 ms | 10,000 ms |\n| Publication/projection time (encoder projects, both trees, in binding) | within binding 335 ms | 10,000 ms |\n| Verification time (binding + project-rows + both derives) | 583 ms | 10,000 ms |\n| Process heap used (whole measuring JVM, Runtime method above) | 193,075,200 B (~184 MiB) | 1,073,741,824 B (1 GiB) used heap, same method |\n| Guest instructions / trace records per C lane | restated, NOT raised | 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 (r1 record) |\n| Binding added guest work | 0 instructions, 0 trace records | 0 (host-side only) |\n\nFailure rule (unchanged): exceeding any ceiling is a failed bounded\nrun; bounds are never silently raised.\n\n## Red-first evidence\n\nTests were written before the fix for each item; observed red in this\nsession:\n\n| Item | Red | Green |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4 (durable) | `repl-packet-provenance-durable-test`: 3 failures (no handles retained; nothing retrievable) | 1 failure (first handle's lane empty — a call-free `def`), then 0 after selecting a call-bearing handle |\n| 5 (binding) | `test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding`: 2 failures (stamped-set equality and stamped>pre-stamp assertions as first written) | 0 (34 assertions) — the stamped set is now verified as marked ∪ derived inserted helpers |\n| 1 (mutation) | with wrapper-removal neutralized in a scratch copy (the pre-r2 behavior), `test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested`: 1 failure (`(get correspondence stamped-path)` = nil for the nested site) | 0 (6 assertions) against the delivered code |\n| 2 (mutation) | with the origin reverted to the content hash in a scratch copy, `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins`: 2 failures (identical origins; identical bound key sets) | 0 (8 assertions) against the delivered code |\n| 3 | new 3-arity admission test written against the root-only signature (its claimed-A/unclaimed-B arm is unanswerable by the old code) | 0 (15 assertions) |\n\nMutation copies lived under `/tmp/cc3-mut/` and were not delivered.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Lane | Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| Callsite battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 34 tests, 389 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Touched semantic + repl | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.derive-test -n yin.repl-test` | 103 tests, 7,601 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Durable store (extra, repl-adjacent) | `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.store-test` | 27 tests, 132 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Oracle binding | `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding` | 1 test, 34 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Oracle nested correspondence | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested` | 1 test, 6 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Oracle distinct admissions | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` | 1 test, 8 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| REPL provenance (individual) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-call-provenance-test` | 1 test, 15 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| REPL durable (individual) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-provenance-durable-test` | 1 test, 7 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| kondo (all 8 changed files) | `clj -M:kondo --lint <8 files>` | errors: 0, warnings: 0 |\n\n## Invariants and unchanged items\n\n- Zero canonical change, legacy loadability, metadata-never-hashed: the\n  r1 assertions still pass inside the suites above; r2 adds no guest\n  instructions and no runtime instrumentation.\n- Datom lane (r1 item 4): restriction unchanged — row lane only, D1's\n  stated dependency; not re-opened by this round.\n- DHT custody (owner-visible, unchanged): `dht/publish-name!` still\n  discards the `:call-sites` handle (now carrying `:provenance`);\n  `dht.cljc` remains forbidden and unedited — the one-line forwarding\n  need stands as recorded in the r1 findings.\n\n## Unverified items\n\n- Full oracle suite and suite-scale battery: shiva at landing (per the\n  original brief); only the three cc3 deftests ran here.\n- cljs/cljd lanes: not run on this laptop; kondo's dual analysis is the\n  evidence (0 errors). The durable-reopen deftest is JVM-gated\n  (`#?(:clj …)`), consistent with the file-store's test precedents.\n- Cold-JVM time ceilings: declared from warm pilot measurements, as\n  §6.3 permits; a cold tagged run that exceeds them is a failed bounded\n  run, not a reason to raise them silently.\n- The kit contract test: N/A on this laptop (r1 record stands).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
